The VAxstation 3100 boot roms (all models) have the well-known
1.073GB limitation - not a problem for NetBSD (apparently)
but not good for OpenVMS.

The VLC has no such limitation (although I expect that there
is another limit somewhere near 256BG ... and there are
SCSI disks getting close to that now). The limitation
it does have is physical size - I fitted a low profile
Fujitsu 1GB SCSI drive into a VLC with no problems.
However, none of the remaining RZ2x series drives I had
to hand would fit - they were too tall.

