Heve you consider IRQ conflicts? What kind of SCSI controler do you
have? If it is PCI card, have you tried to change to another slot? You
can check if there is any kind of conflict if you take a look at
System properties (Start>Settings>Control Panel>System>Device
Manager>Properties) and compare IRQs that SCSI controler and sound
card uses. For ISA SCSI controler you should be able to manually
change IRQ of the controler (either by software setup or by jumpers).
I do have same machine at work, and it works fine (Adaptec 2940UW
SCSI controler), now with NT4 as well as before with W95OSR2 and Win98
Second Edition.


