That is partly correct. I have an RL02 which has a little switch under
the top cover which switches it's behaviour between an RL01 and an RL02.
You can read and write RL01 cartridges, but once written, it will not
be readable anymore by a real RL01 drive unit, unless you re-init the
disk. The reason is is athat the heads of the RL02 have a smaller size
compared to the RL01.

