I'm in the middle of trying to bring up an old PC64 motherboard.  Just
scared up a pair of cache SIMMS that are _supposed_ to be good (these
are the pair that provide 2MB cache and appear to have 10ns chips).
The motherboard works with no cache (jumpers set to disable L2), though
I'm short on memory to actually get an OS loaded.

With the cache simms in place but disabled, the board comes up fine.
If I enable the SIMMs at either 2MB or 512K, at either 10ns or 12ns
(the default for the DEC cache when it was available), the system
fails POST with 6 beeps.  That just repeats every few seconds.

The PDF manuals for this motherboard do not include the POST beep codes.
I haven't had much luck doing a web search either.  Anyone got a list
of the codes for this (Cabriolet, PC64) motherboard?  And any deep
dark how-to-set-up-cache or verify if I got a bad set?  Thanks...

