SBBs, pulled the 9GB drives out, and inserted Quantum QM336700TY-SCA drives
(Altlas II 10k SCSI160 units; be sure to set them single-ended). I'm running
dual-redundant HSZ70s with V7 software.
After a month of solid use, I can report that the Quantum units are reliable
and quite fast on the controller. A stripe of 6 costs about $3600, against
$2710 for *ONE* 36GB SBB (DS-RZ1FC-VW, quoted from Insight).

If you're willing to crack open the SBBs, it's a worthwhile upgrade. Now all
I got to do is order some SCA->SCSI-3 adapters so I can use the old 9GB
drives on some workstations...

P.S. The 36GB Seagate Barracuda SCA drive also seems to work. I had one to
test, and it ran DILX for 24 hrs without any hard or soft failures. It's
several hundred blocks smaller than the Quantum though, and about $50 more.

Dave Schmitt (planning on going from 1TB to 4TB as budget allows...)





