Frank Themann wrote:
> 
> Hello - and a merry christmas to everybody!
> 
> I got an old microvax 3100 server (just one terminal connector...) with
> a single 400MB DSSI hard drive and a tk-70 format tape drive. The
> software I can get in our days usually comes on a CD. How can I add an
> external CD drive to this machine? Are there any SCSI controllers
> available that make CD-ROM boot possible?

There may be some long, semi-cylindrical protrusions on the back of the
unit. These are connector covers. There's a release tab on the bottom of
each - just squeeze it.

There should be 50 pin Centronics-type SCSI connector on the back.
There's also a smaller connector - like a PC parallel printer connector
- you don't want that one.

There should also be more than one MMJ connector on the back, but there
might not be. Those are terminal jacks.

