Can anyone help locate the code that DEC provided for UNIX to see the
I2C bus??  From what I have found I don't think the lm-sensors will
work and it needs the specific DEC code to read the bus.  Any ideas
where else I could post this to find someone that would know is
helpful. Below are my findings so far if anyone is interested.

I think I have been able to locate some of the sensor chips on the I2C
bus.  This is what I have found on the board, there are 3x PCF8584
(interface between micros & I2C bus, so one will be a master the other
two slaves), one PCF8591(I2C, 8 bit, 4x A/D input, 1x D/A output) and a
80C31 (Philips microcontroler) on the main board.  Each processor board
has 2x PCF8574 and one PCF8591 (there are two boards with 2 CPU's on
each), under each CPU(4) there is a "DS1625S" chip which turns out to
be DALLAS Semiconductor's DIGITAL THERMOMETER AND THERMOSTAT chip (they
have a two wire serial bus connection SCL & SDA, but doesn't directly
mention I2C).  I think the DS1625's might have been interpreted as
LM75, since there are 4 of these entries in the sensors program output.

I get the feeling from information I have been able to find that the
80C31 is being used to drive the I2C bus via one of the PCF8584's, so
don't now if this makes it accessible by the kernel or not?  It appears
that DEC had something working for UNIX on these boxes for reporting
this info on top of it just being displayed on the front panel, so must
be possible to get it to work.

From the DEC Manual it gives
"System Management - I2C for reporting of voltage, temperature, PSU
on/off, fan failure, CPU speed."  Haven't been able to find anything
that references how it is done.

From searching on DEC/Compaq site I found this "AMIDiag is a DOS-based
diagnostic program - The I2C test runs only on computers that have the
I2C bus and the Digital 8031 code driving the I2C bus."

It's the last bit "Digital 8031 code driving the I2C bus" that has me
thinking it is specific to the DEC servers rather that a standard I2C
bus driver chip.  Let me know if you think I'm looking at this all
wrong, it was 8 years ago that I actually did anything with the 8031 &
I2C and even then I was looking at cheating using the 80552 that has
I2C built in:).

Running sensors-detect it doesn't find any standard adapters, tried i2c-
elektor first, doesn't find anything on "PCF8584 ISA adapter", then the
Philips-par it just seams to hang with this, the only one that appears
to find any thing is the i2c-velleman which locates the ltc1710,
eeprom, lm75, lm80, adm1021, lm78 sensor chips.  But loading these and
running "sensors" all the values are zero, only one that might see
something is the LM78 which shows "vid: +3.50 V".  From what I have
being able to find out the Velleman is meant for an external I2C board
plugged into the parallel port so not the right one and probably why I
get the message "Busdriver `UNKNOWN'".  Looking on the board I can't
find any of the chips indicated in "sensors-detect" anywhere.

thanks
Steve.




