pzachary <pzachary@sasquatch.com> wrote:
> I need to trade for/buy/make a #3 drive ID plug.
> If somebody has a spare, or can tell me what "bump" configuration I
> need...

Sure you mean "RL03"?  If you mean "RL02" or "RL01" (the plugs are the
same) I had the same problem.  I solved it by pushing 2 matchsticks into
the sides of the switches and working out what the required config was. 

To save you the effort, look at a #1 plug.  There are fingers on the
sides; each finger is trimmed on upper and lower edge to set the code.

For #3, the finger on the right is the same as it is on a #1
        the finger on the left has the upper edge trimmed the same as #1
	the left lower edge trimmed the same as the right upper edge

For #2, the fingers look like a #3 turned upside down.

I made mine out of clear perspex, but any non-conductive material should
do.

