On 18 Dec 2000 19:59:31 GMT, NetBSD Bob
<nbsdbob@weedcon1.cropsci.ncsu.edu> wrote:

>Alas, my ancient and venerable TK50 tape transports are beginning to
>give me read and write errors.  I sense I need to do some deep
>cleaning and some proper tape erasing, if possible.  Anyone got
>any insights or suggestions as to 1) how to properly clean TK50
>tape drives, and 2) how to properly erase TK50 tapes?  mt does
>not have any erase capability, which probably means that the
>tapes are not usually eraseable.  But, I sense I could be getting
>track alignment problems, since many of the tapes do not load and
>position properly at the start of tape.  Others do not write
>well, giving the fast blinking idiot light syndrome, even if they
>do load properly.  A full tape erase would make such problems
>a bit less difficult.

You can clean the drive using a tape drive cleaning kit using foam
swabs and alcohol - Radio Shack sells a kit with these for cleaning
VCRs, it will work fine.  Swab off the head and the capstan.

You can bulk-erase a TK50 tape, but then you have to reformat it - I
don't recommend this.


