robinm@rpi.edu (Michael Robinson) writes:
> As perhaps related, I checked the output of the crystal oscillator
> and the RC oscillator on the M8109.  The xtal one seems not to
> generate TTL logic levels, while the RC oscillator works fine.

The 11/70 uses an M8139 timing generator instead of the M8109.  I
don't have any M8109 prints, but I believe they are very similar.
I hope the following info for the M8139 helps:


In the M8139, the clock mux is E32, a 74S64, and the output is on pin 8
("TIGB SOURCE CLOCK L").

The clock is buffered and distributed to other parts of the machine
as the signals listed below.  There are separate drivers for active-high
and active-low signals, denoted by the "H" and "L" at the end of the
signal name.  For each signal, there is a ground return.  For a signal
"FOO H", the ground return is "FOOR H".

signal    connector    return    connector
------    ---------    ------    ---------
TF H      DM2          TFR H     DM1
TF L      ER2          TFR L     ER1


Most of the machine does not operate directly on the clock, but instead
on divided-down time states and pulses.  However, when the machine is
waiting for something to happen (such as for a memory access to complete),
the timing chain stalls.

There are five active-low time state signals:

signal    connector
------    ---------
TS1 L     CD2
TS2 L     DC1
TS3 L     DE2
TS4 L     ES1
TS5 L     EN1


There are five timing pulses, each offered in both active-high and
active-low.  For each of these there are two drive pins (tied together
on the card), and two ground returns.

signal    connector    return    connector
------    ---------    ------    ---------
T1 H      DT2          T1R H     DR1
T1B H     DS2          T1BR H    DS1

T1 L      ED2          T1R L     EE1
T1B L     EE2          T1BR L    ED1

T2 H      DK2          T2R H     DK1
T2B H     DL2          T2BR H    DL1

T2 L      EM2          T2R L     EM1
T2B L     EP2          T2BR L    EP1

T3 H      DB2          T3R H     DB1
T3B H     DD2          T3BR H    DD1

T3 L      ET2          T3R L     ET1
T3B L     ES2          T3BR L    EU1

T4 H      CR2          T4R H     CR1
T4B H     CS2          T4BR H    CS1

T4 L      FF2          T4R L     FF1
T4B L     FH2          T4BR L    FH1

T5 H      CE2          T5R H     CE1
T5B H     CF2          T5BR H    CF1

T5 L      FR2          T5R L     FR1
T5B L     FS2          T5BR L    FS1


