I have two Celebris XL 5133DP's.  My experience has been that these machines
(Celebris anyway) are fairly touchy when it comes to processors.  For quite
some time I couldn't get my second machine running stable for more than a
few hours.  I finally found the two 133MHz processors were mismatched
slightly, even though according to Intel they should have worked together
just fine.  I located a different set of duplicate (exactly) matching 133's
among my other machines and spares and replaced them.  I have not had a
problem since.  Probably your best bet is tossing in some more memory and
faster drives into your Prioris.  I've found in running web and database
server software on my machines the bottleneck is usually the disk access not
the processor load.  Ben Myers can help you out with a 512K L2 cache, and
more memory should you decide to go that route.

