Richard Jean-Luc wrote:
> 
> Hello,
> 
> I'm currently trying to add a new SCSI disk on a DEC 1000 server.
> As there is no more available slot in the external rack,
> I'd like to disable the DDS1 DAT on SCSI target 5,
> and then insert my new disk in slot 5 of the external rack.
> 
> Should I extact physically the DAT and reboot to free the target 5 ?
> 
> Or is it enough to plug in the new SCSI disk in slot 5 to disable the DAT N
> 
> Does anyone know if that's possible and how ?

I'm not familiar with the particular hardware, but this sounds like a
general SCSI problem.

SCSI requires that all devices connected to the same bus have unique
IDs.

If the DAT drive is installed internally, it's ID is probably set by
switches or jumpers.  You either need to change these switches to an
unused ID or remove the SCSI cable from the drive.

If the DAT drive is in a StorageWorks chassis, you need to change the
SCSI ID switches on the back of the cannister (or just remove the
drive).

