There isn't anything broken.  Mice and keyboards using the PS2 interface are
not really hot-pluggable.  It usually works, but the Mouse/Keyboard HW isn't
really cleanly designed (gosh, it was designed for the old IBM *PS2*).

When the hardware works, the mouse will send a power up sequence, and the
software will re-initialize the mouse.  If it doesn't work the first time,
try, try again.  Most systems I've used, it always works.  I find occasional
systems where I can almost never get it to work - so I assume that the
mechanical connection wasn't "clean" enough for the power up sequence to get
through.

Try unplugging a mouse or KB on a PC :-(

When things eventually migrate to USB, then it will truly be hot-pluggable.

_Fred

