USB is an example of design by committee ;-)   It got some things right, and
some things really, truly wrong.  One thing that should work without problem
is the ability to hot-plug the mouse and keyboard.  But there will be some
interesting problems in device persistance.  Since USB devices do not always
provide serial numbers, and KB/Mice seldom have them on USB - plugging in
more than 1 mouse/keyboard will require topology to identify a specific
mouse or keyboard.  So plugging in new devices, or moving them and changing
the topology will cuase some less-than-amusing problems.  But simple
unplug/replace should work without a problem.

