Can be made to work...
e.g.,
 $ pipe direct /col=1/notra/nohead/siz/wid=file=60 |sort sys$input -
  /key=(pos=60,siz=8) sys$output

You need to examine the output from DIRECT and read HELP DIRECT
to see what you need to do to get it all on one line.

Not sure what use this is, though, compared with the more useful
/SELECT qualifier in DIRECT.

If you want the largest files, rather than wade through a full sorted
list to the end, just use
 $ direct /select=size=minimum=10000  or whatever

Have a good read of the help before investing in something which
will be slow and less useful than what is already there, is my advice.


