They might be either for a DSW42 synch adapter or
possibly a DSH32(?) asynch adapter.

If you open the box you should see the connectors sit on
a logic board at the back of the machine. That board
is connected to another daughter board inside the machine.
The 2-5-2 number on that board will tell you what it is.
On the DSW42 you have to remove the daughter board to
actually see the number - by which tme I'm pretty sure
you can also see either DSW42 or SYNCH I/O in the
etch.

Or you can connect a terminal to the console, power up
and issue the SHOW CONFIG command (or maybe SHOW VER ...
it varies on some models and I don't have one to play
with).

