robinm@rpi.edu (Michael Robinson) writes:
>    I've acquired a PDP-11/45 some time ago, and have been spending
> some time getting it up and running.  However, I've been having
> trouble getting it to do anything at all.  On power up, it 
> appears to light a few random lights and just sits there.  Switching

Is the PAUSE light on?  That indicates a bus hang.

Try setting RUN/HALT to HALT then pressing START.  That should reset
everything.

> Also, do I need another terminator (of M930 type) as the last board?
> I think I do, but nowhere is this specified.  

Yes.  In principle you also need grant cards in all the SPC slots.
If you use an M930 terminator, the CPU should work to some extent
even without the grant cards.  With the newer M9302 terminator, the
grant cards must be present or the bus will hang.  I recently learned
this the hard way on an 11/70, which is basically an improved version
of the 11/45.

> As perhaps related, I checked the output of the crystal oscillator
> and the RC oscillator on the M8109.  The xtal one seems not to
> generate TTL logic levels, while the RC oscillator works fine.  How
> do I specify which one to use?

Where are you measuring?  The important signals are the five strobes
and five timestates, and those should be TTL-like signals but approach
more closely to the positive rail (+5V) when high.

I think the normal way of selecting the RC oscillator is to use a
switch on a maintenance card plugged into a reserved slot.

I've never even been near an 11/45, though, so take all this with
a grain of salt.


