scraft@nothinbut.net wrote:


: I now have a CT450 and two CT475's (to be used as VNC clients).  They
: are all running Win95.
: Some questions for those with real HiNote knowledge:

: How can I make the laptop not sleep when the lid is closed?  I was
: thinking of re-doing one with RH Linux on it and using it as a minor
: server, but every time I close the lid it suspends.

When powering up the CT475, go to setup by pressing Fn-F3.  Somewhere in
there you can set the lid switch to either suspend or desktop/CRT or 
something like that.  Use the desktop setting.

A word of warning regarding the 2.2 kernel and the CT475:  You will have
to patch the PS/2 mouse driver and recompile the kernel, or not use the
trackball at all.  Any use of the trackball will freeze all keyboard and
mouse input forcing either a cold boot or network login to reboot.  I've
never bothered attempting to fix it.

The CT475 is very happy running the 2.0 kernel.  Mine (typing this 
followup on it) runs an older Caldera distribution with the 2.0.35
kernel.  It uses less than half of the 340MB HD and X is snappy enough
with only 12MB of RAM and the C&T65540 chipset.  You will need to force
16bpp at the command line, 'startx -- -bpp 16'.  KDE runs too slowly on
the CT475, don't bother with it.

Good luck with it
-- 
