> linux for the dec5000 hasn't been updated in ages that i know of.

 Hmm, that depends on how you define "updated".  The DECstation Linux port
is actively maintained and is working.  No new drivers for a while,
though. 

> NetBSD and OpenBSD are both quite up to date and well maintained. I'd
> get NetBSD 1.5 for it.

 For regular use, it's probably the best choice.  They are reportedly
stable while the MIPS Linux port (mainly binutils, gcc and glibc) is not
completely stable, yet.  If you want to perform development, choose
whichever you like best. 

