In article <t3347scpvsf5ae@corp.supernews.com>, "Arthur Dalessandro" <adalessandro@odione.com> writes:
>
>I don't see 4.0f, is this an oversight?

I upgraded both of my V4.0F systems to V4.0G a couple of
weeks ago.  I simply didn't have one to build a V4.0F
version.  (Hint, V4.0G is an allowed upgrade path from F,
it isn't just for the GS80/160/320 systems).

The reason I included V4.0E, is that one of those happened
to be available.

I'll also add, since people will probably start to notice it,
that on V5 you may (likely?) notice messages of the form:

monitor: config_disks: No information on dk10: No such device or address.

This seems to be particular to V5.  I use the table(2) system call
to get disk performance data.  The documented interface says that
the first entry of the particular table records the number of
entries in the table.  So, I ask for "how many disks are there"
and then ask for data for that many in turn.  Apparently some of
the entries it claims are there, aren't.  I couldn't decide whether
to silently ignore that particular case or echo the "failure".
Since it only happens at startup, I decided to echo the failure.

