>When the client is V5.0A (and the server V5.0 or V4.0D), I get errors
>(reported on the tty), and in the two files /var/adm/messages and
>/var/adm/syslog.dated/*/kern.log get many lines like
>  Aug 14 11:21:19 venice vmunix: NFS3 RFS3_WRITE failed for server milan: RPC: Server can't decode arguments
>  Aug 14 11:21:19 venice vmunix: NFS3 write error 5 on host milan
>on the NFS client, and lines like
>  Aug 14 11:20:29 milan vmunix: xdrmbuf_getmbuf failed
>  Aug 14 11:21:19 milan last message repeated 176 times
>on the NFS server.

There was a problem with how the client was handling retransmits of
big (>8KB) writes.  It took a couple tries to get it right.

If you mount with -o wsize=8192, I think things will work fine.
Hmm.  This may only be a problem with soft mounts.  If you're using
them, try -o hard,intr (the default).

This will be fixed in the V5.1A release, I don't know the schedule for
patch pools.  Tell your support person that "QAR 83257" is the starting place.

