That is true.  At the time Richie Larry came in and fixed the
microcode on the 11/60 AND the DMC11.  both had the same
harvard architecture base, and Richie stuffed an 8 emulator in 
both.  Actually, the emulator in the DMC and the 11/60 was
about the same speed as the original PDP8e, the design before
july of 70.  Louis Klotz and Remo Vogelsang went back and 
tweaked the timing on the omnibus, and in the M830, 831, 833 to 
allow longer omnibus configs (four x 20 vice two x 20).
The 8 emulator ran quite a bit faster on the KMC11B - 100ns
cycle vice 330ns....
