Paul,

The service manuals for all the Prioris boxes show all the
differences, some with good pictures.  Your best bet is to examine the
motherboards.  If the motherboards are the same, you can swap CPU,
memory and motherboards among them.  If the motherboards are
different, forget about swapping mobo parts around.  The floor model
chassis should be the same among them.  Ditto for power supplies,
drive cages, front panel, side panels, and lotsa other details.

See what you can put together, then let me know what you need.  I have
several decommissioned Prioris HX (and some other Prioris floor model)
boxes here, and I'm willing to part out some of them for reasonable
but not dirt cheap prices.  They are sturdy as tanks... Ben Myers

