Javier Henderson wrote:
> 
>         I'm trying to find what's the size limit for disk drives on an
> AlphaStation 255/300 with VMS 7.2. 

I'm not sure there is a limit, outside of hardware and driver
limitations which seem quite liberal. 18+GB drives are not at all
uncommon, and some people build EXTREMELY LARGE RAID sets and present
them to Alpha/VMS systems with few problems.

>         This is a hobby system, so buying genuine RZ series is out of
> the question.

Rather depends on wther you can live with "small" disks...

I found a guy on eBay selling RZ28B-VAs (circa 2GB) for $40 each. If you
don't have a storage shelf, you can take them out of the canisters and
use them bare (may need SCSI id. jumpers). I've picked up a BA350 shelf
for less than $200US.

Castlewood's Orb (cartridge drive) works reasonably well with OVMS, but
only if you have a way to install the latest firmware update (needs a
DOS machine with a SCSI card). The drive retails around $179.95US and
the cartridges (circa 2.2GB unformatted, 2.05GBF/ODS) are around
$29.95US.

My $0.02US worth...

