> I have got dragged into a project where someone is screen-scraping a
> DECForms project into a Windows GUI and shall we say things are not going
> well, no names, no pack drill.
> 
> I noticed that DECForms supports Motif natively, and being a simple lad it
> seems to me this is a sensible thing to use to get the stuff onto Windows.
> Being a dummy on X-Windows and DECs can anyone:

If what you are wanting is for the DECForms/Motif application to use an
MS-Windows display to allow the MS-Windows user to interact with it then
what you need is to acquire an X server to run on your MS-Windows box.
Once you have that consult its documentation and decwindows documentation
for how to get what you want.

The basic drill something like this:
	a) run the X server on the MS box
	b) configure its authentication mechanism(s) to allow access
	   by your DEC box
	c) bring up a decterm
	d) direct the display to your MS-Windows node with something like:
Set Display /Create/Node="''Node'"/Transport=TCPIP/Server='Server'
	   see decwindows doc for details
	e) run your DECForms/Motif app

For a list of potential X servers see http://www.rahul.net/kenton/xsites.framed.html.

HTH,

-- ced

